    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #164\n\n- 2026-09-16 21:21Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-16 22:07Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #418 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-164-realtime-v1-06-06-implement-client-rec-thr_r5e6hiqd44`. ## Summary Implements the `WS /api/sync` client reconnect and per-stream recovery contract from issue #164. **New package `@semprec/realtime-client`:** - `backoff.ts` — exponential backoff with full jitter, 1s floor, 30s ceiling, doubling per attempt. - `syncClient.ts` — reconnect loop driving each stream's own recovery on every successful connect: resubscribes every open Yjs doc and watched agent run from its own last cursor (no universal cursor), gates new `invalidate` frames behind a one-shot active-state refetch, delivers notifications immediately (never gated), and treats a 4401 session-revoked close as terminal (no further retries). - `docSession.ts` — per-document y-protocols/sync handshake (SyncStep1/Step2/Update), re-run identically on every reopen so a resume after reconnect exchanges only the missing diff. - `serverFrame.ts` — validates every inbound text frame against protocol-v1's closed `OutboundFrame` catalog before it's trusted, mirroring the server's own boundary validation. - Small addition to `@semprec/realtime`: exported `SESSION_REVOKED_CLOSE_CODE` and a few protocol-v1 helpers this new client needs. **Tests:** unit tests for backoff math and the sync client's reconnect/recovery logic against fake sockets and fake timers, plus a new e2e suite (`services/semprec-api/src/__tests__/reconnect.e2e.test.ts`) exercising four real fault scenarios end-to-end — raw network drop, LISTEN connection loss (#242's fault), controlled server shutdown (deploy), and slow-consumer backpressure close — each verifying REST state, Yjs state-vector equality, the agent-event stream, and unread notifications all converge after reconnect. **Verification:** `pnpm run verify` passed in both `backend/` (lint, format, build, 1187 unit+integration tests, 9 e2e tests) and `web/` (lint, format, build, 187 tests) — run synchronously, no failures. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 22:57Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #418 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No remaining local changes to commit — the working tree was already clean. The branch `bb/relay-164-realtime-v1-06-06-implement-client-rec-thr_r5e6hiqd44` is confirmed pushed and up to date on origin (it already backs open PR #418; the earlier push rejection was just my local checkout being behind a `develop`-merge commit that Relay had already pushed to the remote branch — reconciled with a fast-forward, no new work involved). ## Summary Implements the `WS /api/sync` client reconnect and per-stream recovery contract from issue #164 in a new `@semprec/realtime-client` package: - **Reconnect**: exponential backoff with full jitter, 1s floor, 30s ceiling, doubling per attempt (`backoff.ts`). - **Per-stream recovery on every reconnect, no universal cursor** (`syncClient.ts`): resubscribes every open Yjs doc and watched agent run from its own last cursor, gates new `invalidate` frames behind a one-shot active-state refetch, delivers notifications immediately, treats a 4401 session-revoked close as terminal. - **Yjs per-doc recovery** (`docSession.ts`): re-runs the full SyncStep1/Step2/Update handshake on every reopen. - **Boundary validation** (`serverFrame.ts`): every inbound frame validated against protocol-v1's closed `OutboundFrame` catalog before use. - **Tests**: unit tests for backoff math and reconnect/recovery logic, plus an e2e suite covering network drop, LISTEN loss (#242), deploy shutdown, and slow-consumer backpressure — each verifying REST, Yjs, agent-events, and unread-notification convergence. Both `backend/` and `web/` verify pipelines pass in full. Branch: `bb/relay-164-realtime-v1-06-06-implement-client-rec-thr_r5e6hiqd44` Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 23:54Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #418 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully to the existing branch `bb/relay-164-realtime-v1-06-06-implement-client-rec-thr_r5e6hiqd44` (`beada0b..7ef0797`). This push fixes the three correctness bugs both review threads flagged (one with a `FINAL_DECISION: blocked` verdict): - **`syncClient.ts`**: added a per-connection generation id so a stale socket's `onopen`/`onmessage`/`onclose` callbacks can no longer clobber a newer, already-established connection (the reconnect race). - **`syncClient.ts`**: scoped `gateInvalidations` to the connection attempt that set it, so a superseded reconnect's `refetchActiveState()` resolving late can no longer prematurely lift a newer attempt's gate. - **`docSession.ts`**: added `DocSession.dispose()` to detach the `ydoc` \"update\" listener, called from `closeDoc()` before removing the session, fixing the double-registration/double-send bug when a retained `Y.Doc` is reused across a close/reopen cycle. `pnpm run verify` in `backend/` passed in full (lint, format, build, unit, integration, e2e — 9/9 tests green in the affected suites). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-17 00:26Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #418 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Confirmed: local `HEAD` (`e948e2b`) matches remote exactly — the branch `bb/relay-164-realtime-v1-06-06-implement-client-rec-thr_r5e6hiqd44` is already up to date on origin with all commits, including the two rounds of review fixes (reconnect race/gate-scoping/listener-leak, and swallowed-error logging/unchecked-cast guards). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-17 00:29Z — This issue was resolved by #418, which just merged into develop.",
